{"id": 96, "ts": 1784182289.2610414, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I appreciate Agent\u202f1\u2019s confidence in Candidate\u202fA\u2019s reliability and quick decision\u2011making, but I remain unconvinced that those strengths outweigh the gaps we still have on his responsibility, adaptability, and especially his professional communication.\u202fWe know A \u201chas difficulty communicating ideas\u201d and is \u201cregarded as egocentric,\u201d yet we have no concrete evidence that he can translate his technical competence into safe crew interaction under pressure.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB offers clear, documented strengths on the core safety criteria: he is \u201cvery conscientious,\u201d which directly supports operational reliability; he \u201chandles stress very well,\u201d meeting our stress\u2011resilience requirement; and his \u201cgood at assessing weather conditions\u201d and \u201cexcellent computer skills\u201d demonstrate solid technical and cognitive competence for long\u2011distance flights.\u202fWhile B is \u201cpretentious\u201d and sometimes \u201cadopts the wrong tone,\u201d these interpersonal issues are less severe than A\u2019s communication difficulty and egocentric attitude, and they are more amenable to targeted training.\u202fGiven the current evidence, I keep my provisional recommendation for **Candidate\u202fB**, pending any new data on A\u2019s responsibility or crew\u2011cooperation that could shift the balance."}
